// spec: an attribute written before a declaration's `when` (design.md 19) belongs to that declaration, as one written after the condition does: a member declared `[[noreturn]] when (...)` is [[noreturn]], so its definition may not reach its end, and a free function the same
// factorio: CrashHandler's `[[noreturn]] when (config::platform == Platform::Windows) static void createMinidumpAndTerminate();`, the merged configurations' form of a Windows-only declaration: the attribute was dropped (until 2026-11-11), and the definition, which ends with TerminateProcess, was not checked as [[noreturn]]
// error: attribute_before_when_belongs_to_its_declaration.kpp:13: error: terminate is [[noreturn]] and can reach its end: end it with a throw or a call of a [[noreturn]] function
// error: attribute_before_when_belongs_to_its_declaration.kpp:18: error: halt is [[noreturn]] and can reach its end: end it with a throw or a call of a [[noreturn]] function
struct Handler
{
  [[noreturn]]
  when (true) static void terminate();
};
void Handler::terminate()
{
  std::println("terminating");
}
[[noreturn]] when (true) void halt(int code)
{
  if (code > 0)
    throw code;
}
int main()
{
  return 0;
}
